course: dictionary
lesson: 2154
title: Names and money: Cordoba
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cordoba is not an ordinary word, and you will not find it in a plain English dictionary. It is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. Names of places and money can be tricky, because one name can mean more than one thing.
explain: Cordoba can be a city in Spain, a city in Argentina, or the money of Nicaragua. The context tells you which one. «In the 11th century Kyiv was one of Europe's largest cities, but Constantinople, Baghdad, Cordoba and Chinese cities were far larger.» Cities are big places with many people, so here Cordoba is a city.
explain: Always check the clues. Is it a place, a person, or a price? Ask what kind of thing would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning in place of the word to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Cordoba is a name, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: Córdoba is a historic city in southern Spain, famous for its great mosque-cathedral, the Mezquita.
fact: Córdoba is also a big city in Argentina, and it is that country's second-largest city.
fact: A córdoba (with a small c) is the money of Nicaragua.
fact: Córdoba is a Spanish name, not an English word.
exercise: In «Cordoba was one of Europe's largest cities», what kind of thing is Cordoba? | A river | A language | *A city | A type of fruit
exercise: «The córdoba is the money of Nicaragua.» What is a córdoba? | *Money | A famous mosque | A kind of horse | A mountain in Spain
exercise: Why does Cordoba start with a capital letter? | Because it is a name of a place | Because it is a long word | Because it is in the Spanish language, so it always has a capital | *Because it is a name of a place, so it is a proper noun
test: «Cordoba» in a history lesson about Europe a thousand years ago is most likely which? | A sport played in Nicaragua | A famous city in Spain | *A famous city in Spain, and not money | A kind of cake
test: In the sentence «The córdoba is the money of Nicaragua», what clue tells you it is money? | *The words is the money of | The word The | The word córdoba | The word Nicaragua
exam: What is Cordoba in each of these: a city in Spain, a city in Argentina, and the money of Nicaragua? | *Three different things that share one name | Three different kinds of food | Three different things | Three names for the same city
